Package: phaseTime
Type: Package
Title: Haplotype-Specific Phasing of Somatic Mutations and Copy Number Gain Timing
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Kerstin", "Thol", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "kerstinm.thol@gmail.com")
Description: Combines long-read and short-read whole genome sequencing data to
    phase somatic mutations to haplotypes and to estimate the haplotype-specific
    evolutionary timing of somatic copy number gains. Mutations are phased to
    heterozygous SNPs that are physically linked on long reads; SNPs are phased
    to haplotypes using B-allele frequencies in regions of allelic imbalance
    (optionally across several tumour regions); mutation multiplicities are then
    used to classify mutations as early or late relative to a gain, to define
    ancestral copy number states and to estimate the timing of first and
    subsequent copy number gains, including gains placed on the edges of a
    tumour phylogeny. Includes the simulation framework used to validate the
    approach. Implements the methods described in Chapter 6 of K. Thol's PhD
    thesis (University College London, 2024).
